[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-64181"] :question/problem "Find the general solution of the exact differential equation\n\n$$\n2xy\\,\\text{d}x+({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})\\text{d}y=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the differential equation is of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x,y)=2xy$ and $Q(x,y)={x}^{2}-{y}^{2}.$\n\nSince the equation is exact, our solution $u(x,y)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂u}{∂x}=P(x,y),\\,\\frac{∂u}{∂y}=Q(x,y)\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $P(x,y)$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int P(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & =\\int 2xy\\,\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}y+f(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we integrate $Q(x,y)$ with respect to $y.$  Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $x.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{2}-{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}y-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}+g(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComparing the two solutions, we see that we must have\n\n$$\ng(x)=0,\\,f(y)=-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution $u(x,y)=c$ is\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}y-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{3}=c.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-64183/selection/bad137f6453d2bb96426d80ea351515736dd44a7a50657639faf111967d5fd8a" :answer/id #uuid "ae906e1a-0422-52f6-9eda-8c6caee10f95" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x{y}^{3}-3x=-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64183/selection/dea6620f488d6a3743fe72c37156ca1225266ddcfaecb6e3ae390497c1125ad8" :answer/id #uuid "22c4c558-b05e-519b-b063-b30a32c50a21" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{3}y-3{e}^{y}=-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64183/selection/126feabbb10066237b6d152c55aff7bff649e6019608847745c09f22d1c2d2b3" :answer/id #uuid "5101d73b-46f9-599e-8a74-002dce17a18a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}{y}^{2}-{e}^{x-1}+{e}^{y}=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64183/selection/5df0763aa584c3d616ec8ce06e1cbd6ca76af0c34185d627df2794fa8fa166ea" :answer/id #uuid "4fec5da6-9ccd-5867-ad96-dfcd96a40fa8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}y+3{x}^{3}+{e}^{2y}=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64183/selection/6a1f444428d2122430eae01e11a841ded31dff75084de14a4665268c7480011a" :answer/id #uuid "2b4cb3f4-ac37-50e1-b30c-64cf84901e51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{3}y-3x+{e}^{y}=-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-64183/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1a247cc0-c26e-5066-ab1e-59b64168cdd6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-64183/selection/6a1f444428d2122430eae01e11a841ded31dff75084de14a4665268c7480011a" :answer-field/choices ["q-64183/selection/bad137f6453d2bb96426d80ea351515736dd44a7a50657639faf111967d5fd8a" "q-64183/selection/dea6620f488d6a3743fe72c37156ca1225266ddcfaecb6e3ae390497c1125ad8" "q-64183/selection/126feabbb10066237b6d152c55aff7bff649e6019608847745c09f22d1c2d2b3" "q-64183/selection/5df0763aa584c3d616ec8ce06e1cbd6ca76af0c34185d627df2794fa8fa166ea" "q-64183/selection/6a1f444428d2122430eae01e11a841ded31dff75084de14a4665268c7480011a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-64183" :question/id #uuid "3b6e7ffd-24fa-5884-897d-7e3e1edbe5ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-64183" :question/problem "Find the general solution of the exact differential equation\n\n$$\n(3{x}^{2}y-3)\\,\\text{d}x+({x}^{3}+{e}^{y})\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nwith the initial condition $y(1)=0.$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the differential equation is of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x,y)=3{x}^{2}y-3$ and $Q(x,y)={x}^{3}+{e}^{y}.$\n\nSince the equation is exact, our solution $u(x,y)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂u}{∂x}=P(x,y),\\,\\frac{∂u}{∂y}=Q(x,y)\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $P(x,y)$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int P(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & =\\int 3{x}^{2}y-3\\,\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & ={x}^{3}y-3x+f(y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we integrate $Q(x,y)$ with respect to $y.$  Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $x.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{3}+{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & ={x}^{3}y+{e}^{y}+g(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComparing the two solutions, we see that we must have\n\n$$\ng(x)=-3x,\\,f(y)={e}^{y}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution $u(x,y)=c$ is\n\n$$\n{x}^{3}y-3x+{e}^{y}=c.\n$$\n\nThe particular solution specified by the initial condition must have $y=0$ when $x=1.$ These values determine the value of the constant $c.$ Substituting this into the equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}y-3x+{e}^{y}=c \\\\ (1)^{3}(0)-3(1)+{e}^{0}=c \\\\ -3+1=c \\\\ c=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n{x}^{3}y-3x+{e}^{y}=-2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-64183/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4cbd51b4-cbd1-5e18-8c49-44be7967cd38"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-64183"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-103178/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "58827855-4167-5fb9-a8a7-d621ffa996dc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103178/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "2b353dae-641e-589f-90ac-887025e6d2a0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103178/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "7a1c6496-69fd-543b-861c-74f379755198" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103178/selection/343e05bc561f1754cb89989f943a6f3c9344f2abea94d650b67c7b53d017c0c6" :answer/id #uuid "83a84f38-7fa4-5f35-9267-38cccc0737c1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "ÍII only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103178/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "76493e3e-af89-548c-8e13-45db761a7433" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103178/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "63ec2927-e81a-52bb-9f83-5e274ada1c1a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-103178/selection/343e05bc561f1754cb89989f943a6f3c9344f2abea94d650b67c7b53d017c0c6" :answer-field/choices ["q-103178/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-103178/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-103178/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-103178/selection/343e05bc561f1754cb89989f943a6f3c9344f2abea94d650b67c7b53d017c0c6" "q-103178/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-103178" :question/id #uuid "8e4d2f85-2640-5963-a9fc-d023ea35768b" :question/math-academy-id "q-103178" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation:\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nGiven that the differential equation is exact, which of the following functions could be $P(x,y)?$\n\n- $y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-y$\n- $xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)$\n- $y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)$" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nis exact if it passes the exactness test, i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're given $Q(x,y)=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy).$ \n\nFirst, let's differentiate $Q(x,y)$ with respect to $x$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy))=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\n$$\n\nNow, let's apply $\\frac{∂}{∂y}$ to each of the given options:\n\n- First, we check $P(x,y)=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-y.$ This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)-1\\ne \\frac{∂Q}{∂x}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x,y)=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-y$ does *not* give an exact equation.\n\n- Next, we check $P(x,y)=xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy))=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-{x}^{2}y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\ne \\frac{∂Q}{∂x}\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x,y)=xy\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)$ does *not* give an exact equation.\n\n- Finally, we check $P(x,y)=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy))=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x,y)=y\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)$  gives an exact equation.\n\nHence, the correct answer is ''III only''." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-103178/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ed6eeb5-a646-5f47-b6d8-f1078f550376"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-103178"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-318629/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "a9182c8d-53b3-57a3-a556-3c4041973313" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-318629/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "bfa0b0ef-eaeb-525f-97a4-19297b557408" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-318629/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "229f7401-19c6-5cf3-b967-69c635e87901" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-318629/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "59ade000-773d-561c-a0c0-ec271392a826" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-318629/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "65176d1a-1f86-5614-a09f-e09233b335da" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-318629/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "221e44a5-e2c8-56ec-a0d0-c6c30d4dbe67" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-318629/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-318629/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-318629/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-318629/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-318629/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-318629/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-318629" :question/id #uuid "2afce9a3-09a4-5e75-8115-6a50c9574f64" :question/math-academy-id "q-318629" :question/problem "Which of the following differential equations is exact?  \n\n- $({x}^{2}+y)\\,\\text{d}x+(xy+2)\\,\\text{d}y=0$\n- $(3xy)\\,\\text{d}x+({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y=0$\n- $(6y-x)\\,\\text{d}y-(y-4x)\\,\\text{d}x=0$" :question/worked-solution "A differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nis exact if it passes the exactness test, i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's consider each equation:\n\n- The first equation is\n\n$$\n({x}^{2}+y)\\,\\text{d}x+(xy+2)\\,\\text{d}y=0.\n$$\n\n \nTherefore, the functions $P$ and $Q$ are\n\n$$\nP(x,y)={x}^{2}+y,\\,Q(x,y)=xy+2.\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+y) \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂Q}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy+2) \\\\  & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}\\ne \\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\\,\\times \n$$\n\n \nThus, equation I is not exact.\n\n- The second equation is\n\n$$\n(3xy)\\,\\text{d}x+({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the functions $P$ and $Q$ are\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=3xy,\\,Q(x,y)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3xy) \\\\  & =3x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂Q}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}) \\\\  & =2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}\\ne \\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\\,\\times \n$$\n\nThus, equation II is not exact.\n\n- The third equation is\n\n$$\n(6y-x)\\,\\text{d}y-(y-4x)\\,\\text{d}x=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the functions $P$ and $Q$ are\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=-(y-4x)=4x-y,\\,Q(x,y)=6y-x.\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4x-y) \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂Q}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(6y-x) \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nSo,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\\,✓\n$$\n\nThus, equation III is exact.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-318629/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "df3a798c-f226-5b4f-8d65-4a305de2b087"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-318629"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-320578/selection/3a72fd6f915b5d736d230e73ca559cbd3a846feef96d7ed495fac4e59378fbbd" :answer/id #uuid "26d4b2e3-5beb-558c-99c4-5caaa929a501" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{4}{y}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{13}{2}{x}^{2}+22x=c" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-320578/selection/9bee17bc1c3354d1ea5f6e8fc824e972b4928b92f6d235be019fd4e8e5e0c9ac" :answer/id #uuid "2a40792e-9d57-5164-9901-cfe2bf618126" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{{x}^{4}{y}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{13}{2}{y}^{2}+22x=c" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-320578/selection/d9cfbf23fd91a525f6e500cd5696156bbb834d64df9b644f6dc493d5533de371" :answer/id #uuid "3eccf0ad-70e3-5e61-bed7-a03a26cf4e80" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{4}{y}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{13}{2}{y}^{2}+22x=c" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-320578/selection/6d9cb0ac6700ef5e5af549ff48cc6beb6045a57b3652635aa7cb774748970baf" :answer/id #uuid "c10008b3-4dfb-526a-94bf-ee15e22b381b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{4}{y}^{4}}{4}+\\frac{13}{2}{y}^{2}-22x=c" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-320578/selection/61ef38121b87947cd53dba84f1f6fad5a502cf9df693629f9257f810c1604653" :answer/id #uuid "9f73d861-57aa-5a3c-a437-b2e9eb7dfc07" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{4}{y}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{13}{2}{y}^{2}+22y=c" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-320578/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e6fcc765-0309-582c-8738-678dc78cf73f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-320578/selection/d9cfbf23fd91a525f6e500cd5696156bbb834d64df9b644f6dc493d5533de371" :answer-field/choices ["q-320578/selection/3a72fd6f915b5d736d230e73ca559cbd3a846feef96d7ed495fac4e59378fbbd" "q-320578/selection/9bee17bc1c3354d1ea5f6e8fc824e972b4928b92f6d235be019fd4e8e5e0c9ac" "q-320578/selection/d9cfbf23fd91a525f6e500cd5696156bbb834d64df9b644f6dc493d5533de371" "q-320578/selection/6d9cb0ac6700ef5e5af549ff48cc6beb6045a57b3652635aa7cb774748970baf" "q-320578/selection/61ef38121b87947cd53dba84f1f6fad5a502cf9df693629f9257f810c1604653"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-320578" :question/id #uuid "bec2197d-40e8-5881-af2d-3978294960fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-320578" :question/problem "Find the general solution of the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{22+{x}^{3}{y}^{4}}{\\,13y-{x}^{4}{y}^{3}\\,}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We start by rewriting this equation in differential form.\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nStarting from \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{22+{x}^{3}{y}^{4}}{13y-{x}^{4}{y}^{3}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe first multiply through by $(13y-{x}^{4}{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x$:\n\n$$\n(13y-{x}^{4}{y}^{3})\\,\\text{d}y=(22+{x}^{3}{y}^{4})\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nThen, we rearrange the terms:\n\n$$\n(22+{x}^{3}{y}^{4})\\,\\text{d}x+(22+{x}^{3}{y}^{4})\\,\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nNow, we should check for exactness. A differential equation of the form\n\n$$\nP(x,y)\\text{d}x+Q(x,y)\\text{d}y=0\n$$\n\nis exact if it passes the exactness test, i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\n$$\n\nFor our differential equation, we have\n\n$$\nP(x,y)=22+{x}^{3}{y}^{4},\\,Q(x,y)={x}^{4}{y}^{3}-13y.\n$$\n\nNow, let's compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}\\,(22+{x}^{3}{y}^{4}) \\\\  & =\\,4{x}^{3}{y}^{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂Q}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}\\,(x\\,(xy)^{3}-13y) \\\\  & =\\,4{x}^{3}{y}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂y}=\\frac{∂Q}{∂x}.\\,✓\n$$\n\n \nThus, our equation is exact.\n\nSince the equation is exact, our solution $u(x,y)$ must satisfy the following system:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂u}{∂x}=P(x,y),\\,\\frac{∂u}{∂y}=Q(x,y)\n$$\n\nFirst, we integrate $P(x,y)$ with respect to $x.$ Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int P(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & =\\int (22+{x}^{3}{y}^{4})\\,\\text{d}x+f(y) \\\\  & =22x+\\frac{{x}^{4}{y}^{4}}{4}+f(y).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we integrate $Q(x,y)$ with respect to $y.$  Note that the solution should contain an arbitrary function of $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(x,y) & =\\int Q(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & =\\int ({x}^{4}{y}^{3}-13y)\\,\\text{d}y+g(x) \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{4}{y}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{13}{2}{y}^{2}+g(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComparing the two solutions, we see that we must have\n\n$$\ng(x)=22x,\\,f(y)=-\\frac{13}{2}{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution $u(x,y)=c$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{4}{y}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{13}{2}{y}^{2}+22x=c.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-320578/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7bb08d6e-ae86-50f5-8cb4-d7fe50595849"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-320578"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
